            "solution": "1. Natural Brilliance: The nightingale enchanted the marsh with spontaneous, heart-stirring melody.\n2. Insecurity: Instead of trusting her talent, she was dazzled by the frog's pompous claim of being a maestro.\n3. Loss of Authenticity: She allowed the frog to reshape her song, practicing in freezing rain to satisfy commercial ticket buyers.\n4. Fatal End: Exhausted and broken-hearted, her vocal cord burst, illustrating that uncritical deference to commercial critics destroys art.",
